WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.930
The Digital World,

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:06.010
a world inhabited by unusual 
creatures called Digimon.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.950
It has been conquered 
by the evil Bagra Army

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.530
and divided into seven Kingdoms 
ruled by seven Death Generals.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.290
Taiki Kudou has leapt 
into these seven Kingdoms

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:22.060
along with his partner, 
Shoutmon, to save the Digimon.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.630
This is the story of the 
friendship and adventures

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.540
shared by Taiki, his friends, 
and the Digimon.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:56.660
We finally made it to the seventh 
and final Kingdom, Bright Land.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.610
But its ruler, Apollomon, 
had a just heart,

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.360
even though he was a Death General.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.870
My friends and I were torn 
by differing opinions

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.870
because I wanted to trust Apollomon.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.780
Then, just when we all 
trusted each other,

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.450
the evil heart hidden within 
Apollomon, Whispered, was activated.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.650
Then we were thrown by 
Yuu into a dark abyss.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:29.680
<b>Life or Death,</b>

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:29.680
<b>Hell's Battle of the Generals!</b>

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.560
Life or Death,

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.600
Hell's Battle of the Generals!

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.840
Taiki! Wake up, Taiki!

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.780
Thank goodness, you're awake!

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.540
Guys...

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.090
Where are we?

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:48.980
Hell.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.620
You can't mean...

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.400
You're right! This is...

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:06.700
Looks just like hell as humans 
imagine it, doesn't it?

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.110
Is this Bright Land's underground?

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.800
Why would Yuu send us here?

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.840
We still don't know what 
Yuu's team is really after.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.630
Is that... an enemy castle?

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.120
We're investigating it now.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.280
Oh...

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.110
I'm sorry, guys.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.190
Back then...

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.390
<i>Shoutmon! Digivolve!</i>

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.290
<i>Huh?</i>

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.680
<i>I'm not Digivolving!</i>

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.080
<i>I just can't...</i>

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.330
<i>Taiki! What are you doing?!</i>

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:45.220
If I hadn't hesitated, 
we could've used X7 to escape!

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.870
We wouldn't have been thrown down here.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:52.930
This isn't like you, Taiki.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:56.240
Everyone feels uncertain 
in battle sometimes.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.750
Yep. He's right.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.680
No matter what kind of enemy you face,

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.450
it's okay as long as you bounce back!

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.030
You guys...

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.750
That's how it is.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.130
We've already taken these naive 
moments of yours into account.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.830
If I may translate for Kiriha...

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.530
He means, "Don't worry about it."

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.490
I'm sorry, Nene.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.090
You two were right.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.430
Apollomon turned out to 
be an enemy after all.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.750
Nobody could've guessed that 
an evil heart slept within him.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.130
In that sense, I'm just as guilty.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.250
The question now is whether 
we can fight him after this.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.990
Flash... Flash... Flash...

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.990
Come! Come! Come!

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:39.820
That's the signal!

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.300
Let's go.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.470
For some reason, they can't 
transmit messages here.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.370
This way!

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.970
We searched every corner, 
but there's nobody around.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:54.190
So we'll just barge in!

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.290
It really looks like nobody's here.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.250
Yeah.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.340
Man, talk about a letdown!

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.650
We shouldn't let our guard down. 
It may be a trap.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.890
Trap or not, if nobody shows up, 
nothing's going to get started!

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:14.190
Ooh, nice looking throne!

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:16.930
Idiot! Don't do that!

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:22.860
Come on! Let's just 
make this our castle!

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.100
Go ahead.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:27.800
In fact, I prepared this 
castle for you guys, anyway.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.740
Oh, really? So it's our castle!

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.090
Wait... What?!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.550
Yuu!

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.690
What are you doing here?!

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:46.620
An illusion?

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:51.000
Taiki, Kiriha, Sis...

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.630
Welcome to Hell's Field.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:54.800
Hell's Field?

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.780
As the name says, it's the 
hell of the Digital World.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:02.270
A realm of darkness born in the 
shadows of Bright Land's light.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.680
Transmitting messages is impossible here,

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:09.480
except through the crystals in 
the Black and White castles.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.510
Two castles?

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.430
You mean...

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:16.210
I thought you'd get it, Taiki. 
Good guess.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:20.340
You're right. You and I each command 
one of the castles, Black or White,

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.390
located at either end of this realm.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:25.260
Let's settle this here and now.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.130
I challenge you...

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:32.270
with my Team Twilight!

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.690
Oh, boy! Oh, boy!

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.030
Not good.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:03.900
This battle mood in the air 
gives me a bad feeling.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.780
We're obviously going to be 
controlled by that Yuu kid

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.200
and put through all 
kinds of horror again.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.940
Let's get outta here!

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:16.210
What is this realm?

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.480
I'm all excited!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.450
Something is bubbling up in me!

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:23.910
The rules are simple.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.450
We each advance upon the other's castle

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:27.560
and defeat its boss.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.630
Boss? What is the boss?

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:32.490
The boss is the leading 
General of that team.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.800
In other words, me...

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.610
and you, Taiki.

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:42.410
Victory will be declared 
only when one of us dies.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.480
Yuu, what are you...

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.190
There is no escape.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.830
Neither of us can leave this realm

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:54.160
unless the other is defeated.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:57.190
Simple but exciting rules, right?

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.780
What are you talking about, Yuu?!

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:01.940
Do you realize what you're saying?!

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.360
If you lose, you'll...

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.230
It's fine with me. I won't lose.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.970
Besides, it's obvious that your character

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.770
disappears when you lose in a game.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.940
No, Yuu! You're wrong!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.810
Combat begins in five minutes.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:19.440
You can't say "no," but I'll ask anyway.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.980
Do you all accept my challenge?

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.580
Yuu, listen to me.

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:28.450
Yuu!

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.520
Fine. We accept.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:33.390
Kiriha!

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:34.580
All right!

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:36.090
That's the spirit!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.190
I can't wait.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:42.930
Let's fight to our 
hearts' content, okay?

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.170
Hold it, Yuu.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.570
This was your challenge. 
You'd better be prepared.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:50.950
Wow, scary.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:55.710
But, Kiriha, I absolutely won't lose.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.700
This is no game.

00:08:57.700 --> 00:08:58.380
It's a real battle.

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.190
There are no absolutes,

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:03.860
and unexpected miracles can occur.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:06.460
I'm going to teach you that.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:11.360
Kiriha, what are you thinking?

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:15.690
Yuu doesn't think battles in 
the Digital World are real.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:17.000
Isn't that right, Nene?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:20.170
Yes. He thinks even a human's death

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.730
would be just part of a virtual world.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:26.410
But I never thought he'd 
make such a challenge...

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:31.570
Words will never be enough 
to show him that he's wrong.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.920
He has to learn it through battle.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:34.920
That's crazy!

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.800
You're naive as always, Taiki.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.070
We can't count on you to be our leader.

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:43.030
You will follow my lead in this battle.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.030
Wh-What are you saying?

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:47.000
Be quiet and listen to our strategy!

00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:00.910
Men, I am Admiral DarkKnightmon.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.350
The final showdown is upon us at last.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:06.450
The heroes who have fought 
their way through six Kingdoms,

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.690
Taiki Kudou and his friends,

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.340
will soon meet their end...

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:15.090
At the hands of our own hero, 
the strongest of Generals,

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.730
Yuu Amano!

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.230
As you know, Hell's Field

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.770
bears mountains of needles 
forged of the hardest metal,

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.180
flames of intense heat,

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:36.330
and red seas of death that 
will liquefy any Digimon.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.650
It is indeed a realm akin to hell.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:42.790
For them, it will be a 
battlefield of death.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.810
And if we add Yuu's 
strategy to the equation,

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.630
we are truly invincible!

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:57.120
I will now explain our strategy.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.710
Transmitting messages is 
impossible in this realm,

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:03.380
which means the strategy can't be 
changed once it's decided upon.

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:08.880
After analyzing their 
personalities and past battles,

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:11.550
I am certain this is how the 
enemy will approach...

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:19.220
And that's it. 
This formation will be perfect.

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.880
Magnificent, Yuu.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.700
Now, men, onward to battle!

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:28.950
Today we will all, including myself, 
unite as Team Twilight

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:32.340
and present Yuu with victory!

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:42.680
They're coming! Tighten the defenses!

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:44.070
Pawn!

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:47.630
Boing, boing!

00:11:50.190 --> 00:11:54.590
An army of beasts led by 
DarkKnightmon and Lilithmon.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:57.060
They've set the big guns 
on us right from the start.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.230
Kiriha, you're... 
you're sure about this?

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:01.750
Enough!

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:06.550
All right.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.880
DigiXros!

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.760
Shoutmon X5 is here!

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.200
Let's go, guys!

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:28.960
Right!

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.380
Here I come!

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.880
Even your team composition is 
exactly as Yuu predicted.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.840
He truly holds you in 
the palm of his hand.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:45.600
What'd you say?!

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:47.260
Take this!

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.040
Yo, Mr. Sexy!

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:56.620
What?!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.390
This— Ah!

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:01.580
Are you okay?

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:02.760
Yeah...

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:07.100
What?! Her aura is 
different from before!

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.900
Yes, yes, that's right!

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:13.440
It seems this realm is 
perfectly suited to me!

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:15.870
Here you go!

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:21.280
I'll pay you back for all 
that you've done to me...

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.650
You traitor!

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:27.870
That power...

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.390
That's it! Hell!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.810
The hell that humans imagine

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:35.540
is a place where sinners are 
judged for their evil deeds,

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.790
but this is Bagramon's hell.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.030
It's the reverse.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:45.740
Here, all forces of nature favor 
Digimon with evil hearts.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:48.930
But that's...

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.530
What is this?!

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:00.970
Crap! My whole body's gonna melt!

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:02.550
Get out of there!

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.060
I won't let you do that!

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:11.410
We've seen that coming, as well.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.140
Curses!

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:23.450
Apollomon...

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:25.480
No, you're Whispered, aren't you?

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:29.530
We see through all your shallow ideas.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:32.180
All is going according 
to Yuu's calculations.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.220
Go on, play with him, Sethmon.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:38.660
Or will you refuse to heed 
my dark form's orders?

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:41.390
Certainly not. In fact, I am delighted.

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:45.270
I always felt that I didn't get 
to do enough rampaging.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:49.370
You are my true king, Lord Apollomon.

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:50.670
Good.

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:51.770
Let's move!

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:52.770
Yes, sir!

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:59.240
See? It's just like I thought!

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:03.530
When they're cornered, they most 
often rely on a two-part strategy.

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:06.290
Which means Taiki draws the enemy to him

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:10.720
while the vigorous Kiriha 
comes for my head!

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.620
Lord DarkKnightmon handles Taiki's team,

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:16.360
Lilithmon attacks the reinforcements...

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.160
and when Kiriha's team 
tries to take the opening,

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:21.860
Apollomon strikes.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:24.070
A perfect plan, indeed.

00:15:24.070 --> 00:15:25.230
Isn't it?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.760
Okay, Tuwarmon, turn into Damemon now.

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:28.470
What?

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:30.420
It's clear who's going to win.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:33.550
Let's play a different game, okay?

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:34.910
Oh, no!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:38.140
I must remain in this 
style during battle!

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:40.560
I am your bodyguard.

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.150
And... well...

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:45.960
Are you really okay with this?

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.740
If the battle continues,

00:15:47.740 --> 00:15:51.500
you will have to take Taiki's life 
with your own hands in the end.

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:54.340
What are you talking about?

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:57.430
If one of us is beaten, we'll just get 
sent back to our own world, right?

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:58.400
It's just game over.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:00.880
This is...

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:03.340
The Digital World is a dream land!

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:06.400
Here, no matter what I do, nobody dies.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.590
Nobody gets hurt.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:09.390
I can do anything I want!

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:15.570
Sir Yuu...

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:20.180
Oh... Yes, that's right. 
I know, Chuchumon.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:23.400
I've grown a bit attached to Sir Yuu.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:25.220
I must be cool.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.230
Look! We're about to win!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.080
Beelzebumon...

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:45.650
Twin Spear!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:51.850
<i>Strange.</i>

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:55.670
<i>Even though the advantage in 
Hell's Field is overwhelmingly ours,</i>

00:16:55.670 --> 00:17:00.200
<i>I thought Shoutmon X5 would 
be a bit more challenging.</i>

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.100
I'm not finished yet!

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:04.740
It can't be!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:15.280
Just because we've seen 
through all your strategies,

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:17.120
all you do is run away?

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:21.190
All the Death Generals who 
lost to these cowards

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:23.120
must have been fools indeed.

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:29.490
This is how we have won our 
way through to this point.

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.970
By risking our lives on the 
power of our friendship!

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.420
What is it?

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:37.470
There's something strange about 
the way the battle's going.

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:39.870
They're dominating more than I expected.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:46.510
MailBirdramon! 
Why is Kiriha's Digimon here?

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:48.050
Sir Yuu! Are you all right?

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:56.570
Kiriha?

00:17:56.850 --> 00:17:57.640
No way!

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.610
Kiriha should still be somewhere 
in the needle mountains!

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:03.960
Taiki?

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:07.830
Your strategy's fallen through, Yuu.

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:10.370
Why? Why are you here?!

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.290
Like Kiriha told you,

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:14.330
war is not a game.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:17.210
We'll teach you that 
there are no absolutes.

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:20.680
He gave all he had to 
make that happen...

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:25.080
by entrusting his own 
Digimon to my Xros Loader.

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.150
<i>Greymon! MailBirdramon!</i>

00:18:30.150 --> 00:18:32.120
<i>Go to Taiki's Xros Loader!</i>

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:36.840
<i>Head for the Black castle with this.</i>

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:40.600
<i>I think we can handle using 
each other's Digimon by now.</i>

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.700
<i>Maybe we can't Digivolve,</i>

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:45.800
<i>but I'm sure we can DigiXros 
outside our own teams.</i>

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:46.470
<i>But...</i>

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:48.280
<i>Don't talk back!</i>

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:49.970
<i>I told you, I'm taking the lead!</i>

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:53.600
<i>But, Kiriha... the one in the most 
danger will be you,</i>

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:54.710
<i>the one acting as a decoy.</i>

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:57.020
<i>We need Taiki to handle Yuu.</i>

00:18:57.020 --> 00:19:00.120
<i>My gut tells me that.</i>

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.390
<i>Kiriha...</i>

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:03.030
<i>Fight, Taiki!</i>

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:06.260
<i>Shake off Yuu, and your own 
doubts along with him!</i>

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:14.430
Kiriha entrusted his own 
Digimon to someone else?

00:19:14.430 --> 00:19:15.820
That's ridiculous!

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.470
Then what about X5?

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:25.380
You can't mean... My sister did that?!

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:28.580
So I can use X5, too.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:31.820
This is the new power of the 
friendship between us all.

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:35.120
Shoutmon, everyone... do your best!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:36.810
So that's it!

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:39.360
You're not getting away!

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:42.080
Come on, we're going for 
a little swim together!

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:46.600
It can't be! My predictions 
couldn't have been wrong!

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.730
Are you satisfied, Yuu?

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:52.170
Now, stop this battle and come with me.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:55.570
No! It's... It's not over yet!

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:56.990
Hey, hey! Come on!

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:01.030
Reload, Greymon!

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:04.420
Giga Flame!

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:08.550
Will it still work with me, you two?

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:10.200
Of course it will.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:12.360
Kiriha believes in you.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:12.990
All right!

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:17.130
Greymon!

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.500
MailBirdramon!

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.420
DigiXros!

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:26.240
DigiXros!

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.540
MetalGreymon!

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.540
Trident Arm!

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:43.490
He's there.

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.990
Taiki has made it to where Yuu is.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:49.880
Master Taiki!

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.230
What?!

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:56.200
You haven't finished paying 
me back yet, Lilithmon!

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:00.280
We've been had. 
So these were the decoys?

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.540
Back to the castle!

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:10.400
The rest is up to you, Taiki.

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:20.830
Sir Yuu! Sir Yuu!

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:22.830
Yuu!

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:24.540
Nene's waiting for you!

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:38.250
You really are amazing, Taiki.

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:40.220
You're an amazing player.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:45.080
But if I can kill you now, 
I'm the winner.

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:46.480
Right?

00:21:48.330 --> 00:21:49.090
Yuu!

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:58.890
I can't lose.

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:00.480
I don't want to lose.

00:22:00.990 --> 00:22:03.070
It's the final showdown.

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:06.080
The number one General is me!

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:09.690
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:13.210
<b>Digimon Data Collection</b>

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:13.210
Digimon Data Collection!

